{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "anon-009936", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\t# Version comparison\n2\t\n3\tImplement `compare_versions` in `solution.py`.\n4\t\n5\t```python\n6\tcompare_versions(a: str, b: str) -> int\n7\t```\n8\t\n9\tReturns `-1` if `a` has lower precedence than `b`, `0` if equal precedence, `1` if higher.\n10\t\n11\t## Version format\n12\t\n13\t`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, optionally followed by `-PRERELEASE`, optionally followed by `+BUILD`.\n14\t\n15\t- `MAJOR`, `MINOR` and `PATCH` are non-negative integers written in decimal without leading zeros (`0` is fine, `01` is not).\n16\t- `PRERELEASE` is one or more identifiers separated by dots. Each identifier is non-empty and uses only ASCII letters, digits and `-`. An identifier made only of digits is *numeric* and must not have leading zeros (`0` is fine, `07` is not).\n17\t- `BUILD` is one or more non-empty identifiers separated by dots, using only ASCII letters, digits and `-`. Leading zeros are allowed in build identifiers.\n18\t- Anything else (missing parts, extra parts, spaces, empty identifiers) is invalid: raise `ValueError`.\n19\t\n20\t## Precedence\n21\t\n22\t1. Compare `MAJOR`, then `MINOR`, then `PATCH`, numerically.\n23\t2. If they are equal, a version **without** a prerelease has higher precedence than one with a prerelease (`1.0.0-alpha < 1.0.0`).\n24\t3. If both have a prerelease, compare identifiers left to right:\n25\t   - two numeric identifiers compare numerically;\n26\t   - two non-numeric identifiers compare as ASCII strings;\n27\t   - a numeric identifier has lower precedence than a non-numeric one;\n28\t   - if all compared identifiers are equal, the version with fewer identifiers has lower precedence.\n29\t4. `BUILD` is ignored for precedence: `1.0.0+a` and `1.0.0+b` are equal.\n30\t"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "anon-009931", "uuid": "anon-009939", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "C:\\Users\\anon\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agentrun_ne878306\\spec.md", "content": "# Version comparison\n\nImplement `compare_versions` in `solution.py`.\n\n```python\ncompare_versions(a: str, b: str) -> int\n```\n\nReturns `-1` if `a` has lower precedence than `b`, `0` if equal precedence, `1` if higher.\n\n## Version format\n\n`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, optionally followed by `-PRERELEASE`, optionally followed by `+BUILD`.\n\n- `MAJOR`, `MINOR` and `PATCH` are non-negative integers written in decimal without leading zeros (`0` is fine, `01` is not).\n- `PRERELEASE` is one or more identifiers separated by dots. Each identifier is non-empty and uses only ASCII letters, digits and `-`. An identifier made only of digits is *numeric* and must not have leading zeros (`0` is fine, `07` is not).\n- `BUILD` is one or more non-empty identifiers separated by dots, using only ASCII letters, digits and `-`. Leading zeros are allowed in build identifiers.\n- Anything else (missing parts, extra parts, spaces, empty identifiers) is invalid: raise `ValueError`.\n\n## Precedence\n\n1. Compare `MAJOR`, then `MINOR`, then `PATCH`, numerically.\n2. If they are equal, a version **without** a prerelease has higher precedence than one with a prerelease (`1.0.0-alpha < 1.0.0`).\n3. If both have a prerelease, compare identifiers left to right:\n   - two numeric identifiers compare numerically;\n   - two non-numeric identifiers compare as ASCII strings;\n   - a numeric identifier has lower precedence than a non-numeric one;\n   - if all compared identifiers are equal, the version with fewer identifiers has lower precedence.\n4. `BUILD` is ignored for precedence: `1.0.0+a` and `1.0.0+b` are equal.\n", "numLines": 30, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 30}}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "anon-009936", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
